    },
    {
      "id": "iTl3WUMfr630Uek0jHCvs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1929.6922485196833,
      "y": 1271.8712117793755,
      "width": 929.21875,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "at",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 813306934,
      "version": 554,
      "versionNonce": 905181878,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782188638043,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Q1- Option 1 - Inside each microservice\nIt lives inside our application code. Whenever each request comes in, we check and allow or not.\nGood thing is its extremely fast\nCon - No global picture. Suppose user makes 2 requests one goes to Microservice 1 and another to M2,\nboth the M's think it's just one request, and hence due to lack of co-ordination they allow it\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q1- Option 1 - Inside each microservice\nIt lives inside our application code. Whenever each request comes in, we check and allow or not.\nGood thing is its extremely fast\nCon - No global picture. Suppose user makes 2 requests one goes to Microservice 1 and another to M2,\nboth the M's think it's just one request, and hence due to lack of co-ordination they allow it\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "KIbPNSwhdzPOSdoGkRz37",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1929.8986390252821,
      "y": 1456.9852149025892,
      "width": 1060.8984055290575,
      "height": 155.64480069579187,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "av",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1063396458,
      "version": 646,
      "versionNonce": 1280023478,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782189021799,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Q1 - Option 2 - Global Rate Limiter\nThis solves the lack of co-ordination problem\nBut this causes increase in latency - as each request that comes in from a client, it goes through the gateway to a \nmicroservice, which makes a network call to a rate limiter and then processes the request.\nThe latency though is fairly minimal. But this added network overhead can be avoided\n",
      "fontSize": 20.752640092772253,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q1 - Option 2 - Global Rate Limiter\nThis solves the lack of co-ordination problem\nBut this causes increase in latency - as each request that comes in from a client, it goes through the gateway to a \nmicroservice, which makes a network call to a rate limiter and then processes the request.\nThe latency though is fairly minimal. But this added network overhead can be avoided\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
